  "label": "The text 'two sad images from american history' maps onto the visual material depicting the historical illustration.",
  "description": "The text 'two sad images from american history' explicitly labels the bottom visual material (the historical illustration from 'Le Petit Journal Illustré') as part of 'American history,' even though the illustration depicts the Paris Commune, a French historical event. This creates an analogical mapping where the textual entity 'American history' is projected onto the visual entity 'historical_event_paris_commune' (represented by the illustration), misrepresenting its origin and context.",
